        "notes": "No percentage, molarity, aqueous solvent, supplier, grade, excipients or exact equivalence between source lots is established. This bounded qualitative preparation supports source association only; quantitative stock reconstruction and equivalence to a specified acid product remain unapproved. Source-named parts remain UNMAPPED where supplied form or stock identity is not established. MIM_CATALOG references identify only the supported constituent, not approval of that complete owner. Literal 25%, 32% and 35% are retained as source specifications, not normalized comparable fractions. The cited sources do not state a common percentage basis, carrier, grade or assay tolerance; the exact same-or-distinct preparation relation is unresolved. TOGO M2305/M2746 explicitly calls its 25% input concentrated, so that qualitative label does not exclude a numerical percentage. If comparable definitions and assay ranges were established, a real strength difference could be assessed; they are not established here. Before co-installing overlapping candidates, the coordinator must choose an explicit common bounded partial-material scope preserving every source context, or obtain comparable preparation/product evidence. No owner merge or arbitrary winner is selected."
